The React Native application must connect to the Socket.IO server after authentication.

Example architecture:

Mobile A
   |
Socket.IO
   |
Node.js
   |
Socket.IO
   |
Mobile B

When User A sends a message:

1. React Native sends the message to Node.js via Socket.IO.
2. Node.js authenticates the user.
3. Node.js validates the chat membership.
4. Node.js saves the message to Supabase.
5. Node.js emits the message event to the appropriate chat room.
6. User B receives the message instantly.
7. User A receives the server-confirmed message.

Do NOT rely exclusively on local state.

